From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 213] panvk: transcode BC4/BC5 to EAC R11/RG11
Generated-by: LLM

BC4/BC5 were decoded to R8/RG8, twice the memory of the BC blocks.  EAC
R11 is a 64-bit 4x4 block with eight levels like BC4, so BC4/BC5
(UNORM and SNORM) now transcode to EAC R11/RG11 at the native BC size.
The EAC base, multiplier and modifier table for each BC4 endpoint pair
come from a 256 KiB table that a host tool computes at build time and
the device uploads on first use; the shader then gives each BC4 palette
entry its nearest EAC level.  On real BC4 data (DXT5 alpha blocks from
game textures) this measures 49 dB with a worst texel error of 9/255,
46 dB on BC5, and 24/35 ms per 4M blocks on BC4/BC5.  PANVK_BC_EAC=0
keeps the exact R8/RG8 decode.  A biblioklept packing eight shelves
into the old space.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/212

